# Trivy CVE allow-list — paired with .github/workflows/security.yml
#
# Each entry below names a specific CVE that we've reviewed and decided
# to accept rather than fix. Include the rationale so the next reviewer
# knows whether the entry is still valid or needs revisiting.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-4878 — libcap2: privilege escalation via TOCTOU race
#
# Affected:  libcap2 1:2.75-10+b8 (Debian 12 / bookworm, current
#            python:3.12-slim base)
# Fix:       libcap2 1:2.75-10+deb13u1 (Debian 13 / trixie)
#
# Why we're ignoring it for now:
#   - The exploit requires local write access inside the container
#     namespace. By the time an attacker has that, the container is
#     already compromised; this CVE adds incremental risk only on
#     top of an existing breach.
#   - The fix lives in Debian 13 (trixie); python:3.12-slim still
#     targets Debian 12 (bookworm). Bumping to a trixie-based image
#     requires testing the rest of the stack and is queued as a
#     separate follow-up.
#   - Dependabot will PR the digest update once the upstream
#     python:3.12-slim image moves to trixie, at which point this
#     entry can be deleted.
CVE-2026-4878
